>> title: Caesar Dressing
>> category: Dressings & Dips
>> tags: salad, anchovy, parmesan, garlic, no-cook
>> counters: Deli, Pizzeria, The Bowl Shop
>> aka: caesar salad dressing, creamy caesar
>> servings: 8
>> time: 15 min
>> slack: unforgiving — the oil goes in slowly or it splits and will not come back, and raw yolk makes it a three-day fridge item

>> step: mash to a paste
Mash @garlic{2%cloves} and @anchovy fillets{4}(oil-packed) with @kosher salt{1/2%tsp} to a paste in a #mortar{}.

>> step: whisk in
Whisk @egg yolks{2%large}, @lemon juice{2%Tbs}(30 mL), @dijon mustard{1%tsp}, and @Worcestershire sauce{1/2%tsp} into @&(~1)garlic paste{}.

>> step: stream in, whisk to emulsify
Stream @extra-virgin olive oil{2/3%cup}(160 mL) into @&(~1)base{} in a thin thread, whisking until thick.

>> step: stir in
Stir @parmesan{1/3%cup}(30 g; finely grated) and @black pepper{1/2%tsp} into @&(~1)dressing{}.
